{"title":"Desert Dairy","sub":"Should a dairy company build a new plant?","type":"Investment / capacity","industry":"Food manufacturing","geo":"Saudi Arabia","diff":2,"fmt":"Candidate-led","time":"30-35 min","skills":"Demand vs capacity · timing · cheaper alternatives first","prompt":"Desert Dairy is a leading dairy producer in Saudi Arabia. Its one plant can produce 500 million litres a year and is running at 460M litres. Demand is growing ~7% a year. The board is considering a new $150M plant that would add 200M litres of capacity. Should they build it?","clarify":[{"q":"Profit per litre?","a":"Contribution ≈ $0.30 per litre."},{"q":"Construction time?","a":"About 3 years from decision to production."},{"q":"Other options?","a":"Engineers say $20M of upgrades could squeeze 60M more litres from the existing plant within a year."},{"q":"Competitors?","a":"Two competitors have also announced expansions."}],"structure":{"root":"Build a new plant?","branches":[{"head":"Demand","items":["Our growth vs market growth","Is 7% sustainable?","Product mix"]},{"head":"Supply","items":["Our capacity & upgrades","Competitor capacity → price risk","Outsourcing to co-packers"]},{"head":"Economics","items":["Investment, contribution, payback","Timing vs 3-year build"]},{"head":"Risks","items":["Overcapacity","Execution","Raw milk supply"]}]},"hypothesis":"They will need more capacity, but the cheap upgrade should come first. The real question is when to commit to the new plant, given the 3-year build.","questions":[{"q":"When does Desert Dairy run out of capacity?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<table class=\"data mini\"><tr><td>Year</td><td class=\"r\">0</td><td class=\"r\">1</td><td class=\"r\">2</td><td class=\"r\">3</td><td class=\"r\">4</td><td class=\"r\">5</td></tr> <tr><td>Demand (M litres, +7%/yr)</td><td class=\"r\">460</td><td class=\"r\">492</td><td class=\"r\">527</td><td class=\"r\">564</td><td class=\"r\">603</td><td class=\"r\">645</td></tr></table> <p>Current plant (500M) runs out in <b>year 2</b>. With the $20M upgrade (560M) it's enough until <b>year 3</b>, when demand reaches 564M. A new plant takes 3 years, so <b>the decision has to be made now</b> to have capacity by year 3-4.</p>"},{"q":"Is the $20M upgrade worth it?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Extra volume sold: year 2 ≈ 27M litres (527 − 500) → $8M; year 3 onwards the full 60M litres → $18M/yr. Payback ≈ <b>2.5–3 years</b> from today ($0 in year 1, $8M in year 2, $18M in year 3), even if the new plant later takes over this volume. Easily worth it, and it buys time.</p>"},{"q":"Here is the industry picture. Does this change anything?","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"348.145pt\" height=\"196.548pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 348.145 196.548\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style></defs><g id=\"figure_1\"><g id=\"patch_1\"><path d=\"M 0 196.548 L 348.145 196.548 L 348.145 0 L 0 0 L 0 196.548 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"axes_1\"><g id=\"patch_2\"><path d=\"M 28.465 171.44 L 340.945 171.44 L 340.945 27.296 L 28.465 27.296 L 28.465 171.44 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"><g id=\"xtick_1\"><g id=\"line2d_1\"><defs><path id=\"mff7d576334\" d=\"M 0 0 L 0 3.5 \" style=\"stroke: #555555; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></defs><g><use xlink:href=\"#mff7d576334\" x=\"105.795909\" y=\"171.44\" style=\"fill: #555555; stroke: #555555; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_1\"><g style=\"fill: #555555\" transform=\"translate(93.172706 187.134) scale(0.09 -0.09)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-2f\" d=\"M 269 4678 Q 269 4710 285 4729 Q 301 4749 346 4749 L 3789 4749 Q 3827 4749 3846 4729 Q 3866 4710 3866 4678 L 3866 4346 Q 3866 4282 3789 4282 L 2490 4282 Q 2419 4282 2419 4218 L 2419 83 Q 2419 0 2342 0 L 1882 0 Q 1805 0 1805 83 L 1805 4211 Q 1805 4282 1741 4282 L 346 4282 Q 269 4282 269 4346 L 269 4678 z\n