2 0 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-17\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-5c\" transform=\"translate(29 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-46\" transform=\"translate(87.40625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-6d\" transform=\"translate(147.3125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-6a\" transform=\"translate(205.21875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-6c\" transform=\"translate(255.125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-69\" transform=\"translate(293.828125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-75\" transform=\"translate(332.125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a5\" transform=\"translate(385.125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-46\" transform=\"translate(406.53125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-48\" transform=\"translate(466.4375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-5b\" transform=\"translate(524.53125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-3b\" transform=\"translate(615.125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-5c\" transform=\"translate(669.921875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-46\" transform=\"translate(728.328125 0)\"/></g></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"pa634a78e4c\"><rect x=\"28.465\" y=\"27.296\" width=\"312.48\" height=\"144.144\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Saudi dairy capacity vs demand, billion litres (case data)","note":"Includes competitors' announced expansions, but not Desert Dairy's new plant."},"answer":"<p>Industry capacity grows 25% while demand grows ~23%. Utilisation is ~87% today and stays ~85% in three years even before our plant. Adding 0.2bn more would push it to ~81%. <b>So-what:</b> more capacity → pressure on prices. Model a lower contribution (e.g. $0.25/litre) for the new plant's volume, and consider building it in phases.</p>"}],"reco":"Do the $20M upgrade immediately: it pays back in under 3 years and covers demand until year 3. Approve the new plant now because of the 3-year build, but in two phases (e.g. 100M litres first), because competitors are also expanding and prices may come under pressure. Use co-packers to cover any short-term peaks. Next steps: firm up raw-milk supply contracts, and rerun the plant economics at $0.25/litre.","great":["Builds the demand table year by year","Spots that the 3-year build forces the decision now","Tries the cheaper option first","Considers competitor supply and prices, not only our own demand"],"id":8,"slug":"desert-dairy"}